---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../../config';
import { path } from '../../i18n';
---

<Legal
  lang="en"
  page="deleteAccount"
  title="Delete Account and Data"
  description="How to delete all Tanukonomy data from your device, and the planned account deletion process once accounts are available."
>
  <p class="lede">
    <strong>Tanukonomy doesn’t have an account system yet.</strong> Everything you record — wallets, transactions,
    budgets, freelance projects — is stored only on your own device, never sent to any server. So right now there’s no
    “account” to delete; what you can delete is the data itself, directly on your device.
  </p>

  <h2>1. How to delete all your data now</h2>
  <p>Pick one:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Uninstall the app.</strong> Long-press the Tanukonomy icon, choose “Uninstall”, and confirm. This
      permanently and immediately deletes every wallet, transaction, budget, and setting.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Clear the app’s data without uninstalling.</strong> Open Android Settings → Apps → Tanukonomy → Storage
      → Clear data (wording varies by Android version). The app stays installed but resets to a freshly-installed
      state.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. What data is deleted, and for how long</h2>
  <p>
    Because Tanukonomy has no server, there is no copy of your data anywhere but your device. As soon as you do either
    of the above:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Deleted immediately, with no retention period</strong>: every wallet and its balance, transaction
      history, budgets and their items, freelance projects and hours, and app settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Nothing is kept by us afterward</strong> — we have no way to recover, view, or share data you’ve
      deleted, because we never held a copy of it in the first place.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your operating system’s own backup (such as Google backup on Android), if you’ve turned it on, is managed by
    Google under their own policies — see <a href={path('privacy', 'en')}>Privacy Policy</a> §4.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Once accounts are available (not active yet)</h2>
  <p>
    We plan to add an optional account for syncing across devices and a premium plan — see{' '}
    <a href={path('privacy', 'en')}>Privacy Policy</a> §6. This feature is <strong>not available yet</strong>. Once it
    goes live, this page will be updated with the exact steps, following these commitments:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>account deletion will be available <strong>inside the app</strong> (Settings → Account → Delete Account),
      with no need to contact us first;</li>
    <li>deleting your account will remove your data from our servers within <strong>30 days</strong> of the
      request;</li>
    <li>data stored locally on your device is not automatically deleted by an account deletion — use the steps in §1
      if you want to remove that too;</li>
    <li>if in-app deletion isn’t possible for some reason, a request by email below will be processed on the same
      timeline.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Other questions or requests</h2>
  <p>
    Send them to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Mention your device and, if relevant, roughly
    when you installed Tanukonomy, so we can help faster.
  </p>
</Legal>
